[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Vienna Game"]
[Variation "Vienna Game: Vienna Gambit, 3...exf4 4.e5"]
[ECO "C26"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "space,development-lead"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "3...exf4"]
[Start "1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. f4 exf4 4. e5"]

4... Ng8 ( 4... Ne4 5. Nxe4 { Black's knight went forward with nothing behind it, so White just wins a piece. } 5... d6 6. d4 ) ( 4... Nh5 5. Qxh5 { The knight is simply lost, so the queen takes it. } 5... Nc6 6. Bc4 ) 5. Nf3 { Develops and stops ...Qh4+. White is a pawn down but the pawn on e5 cramps Black. } 5... d6 ( 5... Nc6 6. d4 { Takes the centre; the pawn on e5 cramps Black. } 6... d5 7. Bxf4 ) 6. d4 { Opens the bishop on c1 so that Bxf4 can win the pawn back, and challenges the pawn on e5. } 6... dxe5 ( 6... Be7 7. Bxf4 ) 7. Qe2 { Attacks the pawn on e5. Taking it with the knight runs into ...Qh4+, so the queen does it. } 7... Be7 8. Qxe5 { Wins the pawn back with the queen centralised; the black king still sits in the middle. } 8... Nf6 9. Bxf4 { The second pawn is won back, so material is level and White has the better development. } 9... c6 10. O-O-O { Castles long so the rook joins the fight on the d-file at once. Plan: pressure the pawn on d6 and the black king with Qe5, Bd3 and Rhe1. } 10... Nbd7 *
